description:
Now the closure environment of `peek_vars` for instance is not the namespace but a child of the namespace.

This is not wrong as it is but I believe it's not useful since there's nothing in the closure environment, it would nicely print "<environment: namespace:tidyselect>" if the environment was set to the namespace. 

Given functions like `peek_vars` are reexported in dplyr that also makes it easier to understand what package they're from.

``` r
tidyselect::peek_vars
#> function (..., fn = NULL) 
#> {
#>     if (!missing(...)) {
#>         ellipsis::check_dots_empty()
#>     }
#>     x <- vars_env[[what]]
#>     if (is_null(x)) {
#>         if (is_null(fn)) {
#>             fn <- "Selection helpers"
#>         }
#>         else {
#>             fn <- glue::glue("`{fn}()`")
#>         }
#>         abort(glue_c("{fn} must be used within a *selecting* function.", 
#>             i = "See <https://tidyselect.r-lib.org/reference/faq-selection-context.html>."))
#>     }
#>     x
#> }
#> <bytecode: 0x00000000110a2028>
#> <environment: 0x00000000110a2e28>
```

I think the fix is something like this :

```
peeker <- function (what) 
{
  res <- function(..., fn = NULL) { # <----------  assign to res
    if (!missing(...)) {
      ellipsis::check_dots_empty()
    }
    x <- vars_env[[what]]
    if (is_null(x)) {
      if (is_null(fn)) {
        fn <- "Selection helpers"
      }
      else {
        fn <- glue::glue("`{fn}()`")
      }
      abort(glue_c("{fn} must be used within a *selecting* function.", 
                   i = "See <https://tidyselect.r-lib.org/reference/faq-selection-context.html>."))
    }
    x
  }
  environment(res) <- parent.frame() # <----------  change environment
  res
}
```
